Here is the exhaustive, complete list of every single key name recognized by the Python keyboard library.
## Alphanumeric & Symbols

* a through z: Lowercase letters (always use lowercase; capitalization is handled via shift).
* 0 through 9: Main keyboard row numbers.
* space: Spacebar.
* -: Hyphen / Minus.
* =: Equals sign.
* [: Left square bracket.
* ]: Right square bracket.
* ;: Semicolon.
* ': Apostrophe / Single quote.
* ,: Comma.
* .: Period / Full stop.
* /: Forward slash.
* \: Backslash.
* `: Backtick / Grave accent.

## Modifiers & System Controls

* alt or left alt: Left Alt key.
* right alt: Right Alt key (AltGr).
* ctrl or left ctrl: Left Control key.
* right ctrl: Right Control key.
* shift or left shift: Left Shift key.
* right shift: Right Shift key.
* windows or cmd: Windows key / Command key.
* right windows or right cmd: Right-side OS key.
* menu: Context menu application key (next to right Ctrl).
* caps lock: Caps Lock toggle.
* num lock: Num Lock toggle.
* scroll lock: Scroll Lock toggle.

## Editing & Navigation

* enter or return: Main Enter key.
* tab: Tabulation key.
* backspace: Backspace key.
* esc or escape: Escape key.
* up: Up arrow.
* down: Down arrow.
* left: Left arrow.
* right: Right arrow.
* page up: Page Up.
* page down: Page Down.
* home: Home key.
* end: End key.
* insert: Insert key.
* delete: Delete key.

## Function Keys

* f1 through f24: All twenty-four possible system function keys.

## Dedicated Numeric Keypad (Numpad)

* num 0 through num 9: Numpad numbers.
* num decimal or num .: Numpad period.
* num enter: Numpad Enter key.
* num add or num +: Numpad plus.
* num subtract or num -: Numpad minus.
* num multiply or num *: Numpad asterisk.
* num divide or num /: Numpad slash.
* clear: Dedicated Numpad clear key (on some layouts).

## Audio & Multimedia Buttons

* play/pause media: Play or pause media playback.
* stop media: Stop media playback.
* next track: Skip to the next track.
* previous track: Rewind to the previous track.
* volume up: Turn system volume up.
* volume down: Turn system volume down.
* volume mute or mute: Mute system audio.

## Miscellaneous Diagnostic Keys

* print screen or prtscn: Print Screen key.
* pause or break: Pause/Break key.
* help: Help key (found on select keyboards).
* sleep: System sleep key.

------------------------------
## How to use these names in code
You can instantly use any name from this list inside your automation functions:

import keyboard
# Press a shortcut combination
keyboard.press_and_release('ctrl+shift+esc')
# Block a specific key from functioning
keyboard.block_key('num 5')
